    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hpu/jobs/5445039/assistant-vp-of-treasury-and-financial-services": {
      "title": "Assistant VP of Treasury and Financial Services",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Career Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant VP of Treasury and Financial Services | Career Opportunities page has loaded. Assistant VP of Treasury and Financial Services | Career Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant VP of Treasury and Financial Services Print Apply ﻿ Assistant VP of Treasury and Financial Services Salary $140,000.00 - $160,000.00 Annually Location Waterfront Plaza, Honolulu, Hawaii Job Type Staff - Executive Job Number 02743 Department CFO Administration Opening Date 08/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Hawai‘i Pacific University is designated as an Alaskan Native and Native Hawaiian (ANNH) Serving Institution by the US Department of Education. As such, we strive for accurate displays of the Hawaiian language in all our institutional materials. This includes the appropriate use of diacritical marks such as the ‘okina and kahako. Unfortunately, at times external vendors and other third-party technology integrations do not support the use of these characters. Mahalo for your understanding. Description Job Summary: Reporting directly to the Senior Vice President and Chief Financial Officer, the Assistant Vice President, Treasury and Financial Services is a senior finance leader responsible for overseeing the University’s treasury operations, student accounts, bond portfolio, investment liquidity, and the flow of externally sponsored funds. This position plays a critical role in safeguarding institutional liquidity, strengthening cash management practices, supporting regulatory and audit compliance, and ensuring sound stewardship of University financial resources. The AVP provides strategic and operational leadership for Student Accounts, treasury and banking operations, oversight of the University’s bond portfolio, and investment liquidity management. In addition, this role provides financial leadership for Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP) audit coordination and funds flow, ensuring alignment with sponsor requirements, internal controls, and University policies. The position serves as a key member of the CFO’s leadership team and interacts regularly with executive leadership, external auditors, banks, bond advisors, investment managers, and other financial counterparties. Location : This on-site position will sit in the Business Office at our Waterfront Plaza campus site in downtown (Ala Moana) Honolulu. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, business, or a related field; and/or Minimum seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in treasury, finance, accounting, or financial services. Knowledge of accounting systems and internal control requirements. Thorough knowledge of GAAP, fund/governmental accounting practice and principles, and Accounting Standards Codification (ASC). Demonstrated experience overseeing cash management, banking relationships, and liquidity forecasting. Strong analytical, written, and oral communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, and Outlook Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree in finance, accounting, business administration, or a related field. Experience in higher education or a complex nonprofit organization. Experience with debt management, bond financing, or interaction with rating agencies and bondholders. Familiarity with sponsored program funding, compliance, and audit requirements. Experience with enterprise financial systems (e.g., Ellucian Banner) and banking platforms. CPA, CFA, or similar professional credential. Other Qualifications: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States.  Visa sponsorship and relocation allowance are not available for this position. Report to work obligations to support the department and may require work during HPU’s winter break, if necessary. This position may be considered an essential position with report to work obligations depending on the type of emergency, campus closure, or evacuation. Must meet training and background check qualifications and comply with the Protection of Minors policy. Upon hire, must maintain reliable personal transportation to facilitate travel between to all HPU worksites and other locations as required by the position.   This includes a valid driver’s license and a personal vehicle that is legally registered and insured. Able to work all shifts and extended hours, as applicable. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment requiring excellent time and stress management skills. Key Responsibilities/Essential Job Functions: Treasury and Liquidity Management (40%) Provide integrated oversight of the University’s treasury functions, bond portfolio, and investment liquidity, including cash positioning, liquidity forecasting, monitoring covenant compliance and continuing disclosure requirements, and ensuring adherence to investment policies. Coordinate with the CFO, bond counsel, financial advisors, banks, investment managers, and external auditors on treasury, debt, and liquidity-related matters. Direct short-term investment and liquidity strategies to optimize safety of principal, liquidity, and yield in alignment with University policy and operational needs. Prepare analyses and materials related to treasury performance, debt service and refinancing opportunities, liquidity sufficiency, and long-term debt and liquidity strategy. 2. Student Accounts Oversight (30%) Provide strategic and operational leadership for Student Accounts, including billing, receivables, collections, refunds, and customer service operations. Ensure student account processes support enrollment and student success while maintaining sound internal controls. Collaborate closely with Enrollment Management, Financial Aid, and Academic Affairs on policies and practices affecting student financial obligations. Monitor receivables, aging, and cash collections; develop strategies to improve collections and reduce outstanding balances. 3. Office of Sponsored Program (OSP) – Audit & Flow of Funds (15%) Provide financial oversight for the flow of sponsored program funds in coordination with the Office of Sponsored Programs and the Controller’s Office. Support audit readiness and compliance related to sponsored programs, including Uniform Guidance requirements. Ensure timely and accurate financial reporting, drawdowns, reconciliation, and closeout of sponsored funds. 4. Talent Development & Leadership (10%) Collaborate closely with the AVP Controller, AVP Financial Planning, and other finance leaders to ensure alignment across financial functions. Build, lead, and retain high-performing teams to support organizational goals and institutional priorities. Supervise and manage direct report(s) to drive engagement, accountability, and alignment with the University’s mission, vision, values, code of conduct, and division/department objectives. Promote professional development, succession planning, and personal growth through ongoing coaching, mentoring, and timely feedback. Conduct regular performance discussions; proactively address performance or conduct concerns; document issues; and consult with Human Resources as appropriate. Complete annual performance review processes by established deadlines, including goal setting, progress discussions, and formal evaluations. Serve as a role model by leading with integrity, professionalism, and openness to feedback. 5. Other Duties and Special Projects (5%) Actively participates as an effective member of team by completing assigned duties, accepting additional assignments or reassignments. Assists with seasonal peaks. Prepare analyses, reports, and materials for senior leadership and Board committees as requested. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University’s mission and strategic objectives. This description is not designed to list all activities, duties or responsibilities which may be required for this job. Other duties, responsibilities and activities may be assigned at any time. Hawaii Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a diverse, equitable environment in which faculty and staff can excel irrespective of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, or any other protected class covered by state and federal law. Hawaii Pacific University encourages applications from veterans and individuals with disabilities. A pre-employment background investigation is performed on candidates selected for employment. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants, including individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), reasonable accommodations are available throughout the application and hiring process. If you require an accommodation, please contact hr@hpu.edu to request assistance. Hawai'i Pacific University is a learning community where staff, faculty, and more than 5,000 students come together from around the world to learn and work in a spirit of caring, honesty, freedom, and 'ohana (family). Cooperation, communication, and collegiality are the foundation of our community. We fulfill the responsibilities of our educational mission through mutual trust and respect, innovation and involvement, expertise, and intellectual fellowship. We offer all members of our community the opportunity to excel, including resources and rewards commensurate with individual contributions and potential. As a team, we are committed to serving our local and global communities and embrace our values of aloha, pono, and kuleana. We seek talented and energetic people who thrive on challenge and innovation in supporting the mission and values of our university. HPU offers competitive compensation and a comprehensive benefits package. For student employment, please visit Career Development Center . Why consider a career with HPU?  Here are some of the benefits of employment . . . Time Off A generous schedule that recognizes 15 holidays annually, plus winter break days off between Christmas and New Year's.  Eligible employees also receive vacation, sick and other types of paid leave. Tuition Waiver Full time employees and spouse/dependent children pursuing a higher education degree at HPU may apply for a tuition waiver. Health and Wellness Comprehensive health insurance, life and disability insurance, employee assistance program and wellness program. Retirement Plan Eligible employees can start saving for the future and enroll in the Hawai'i Pacific University 403(b) retirement plan upon hire. Discounts Discounts for products and services including airlines, rental car, hotels, theme parks, attractions, gift cards, restaurants, and more. 01 Do you have a bachelor's degree in finance, accounting, business, or a related field, and/or at least seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in treasury, finance, accounting, or financial services? Yes No 02 Do you have professional experience working with accounting systems and internal control processes? Yes No 03 Do you have professional experience applying Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), fund/governmental accounting principles, and Accounting Standards Codification (ASC) standards? Yes No 04 Do you have experience overseeing cash management, banking relationships, and liquidity forecasting? Yes No 05 Do you have professional experience requiring regular written and verbal communication with internal and external stakeholders? Yes No 06 Do you have professional experience using Microsoft Excel, Word, and Outlook? Yes No Required Question Employer Hawaii Pacific University Address Waterfront Plaza 500 Ala Moana Blvd Ste 4-545 Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Phone 8085441188 Website http://www.hpu.edu/jobs Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, inclu