      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Career Opportunities Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Applications Administrator I | Career Opportunities page has loaded. Applications Administrator I | Career Opportunities page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Applications Administrator I Print Apply ﻿ Applications Administrator I Salary $49,680.00 - $60,030.00 Annually Location Pioneer Plaza, Honolulu, Hawaii Job Type Staff - Regular Full Time Exempt Job Number 02760 Department Information Technology SVC Opening Date 09/09/2026 Description Benefits Questions Hawai‘i Pacific University is designated as an Alaskan Native and Native Hawaiian (ANNH) Serving Institution by the US Department of Education. As such, we strive for accurate displays of the Hawaiian language in all our institutional materials. This includes the appropriate use of diacritical marks such as the ‘okina and kahako. Unfortunately, at times external vendors and other third-party technology integrations do not support the use of these characters. Mahalo for your understanding. Description Job Summary: This position will work within the Enterprise Applications and Data Management team to support one of the University’s core business areas as a direct consult and subject matter expert (e.g. SIS, FIS, HRIS or ERP General specialist). The Application Administrator will develop solutions to help manage business processes, write specifications, and provide documentation for necessary changes. This person will be responsible for resolving non-routine problems as they arise, serving as a resource, translating technical information to non-technical users, analyzing software applications that can enhance office operations, maintaining data integrity and provide training when the need arises. The position includes responsibilities for systems migration testing, writing scripts and resolving system integration issues in collaboration with HPU’s central Information Technology Services Department and end users. Location : This position is based out of our Pioneer Plaza campus site in downtown Honolulu. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science , Management Information Systems, Business Administration, or a related field; or 3 years of relevant IT experience in lieu of a degree. Experience working within fully integrated systems, which may include applications, databases, and application program interfaces. Experience administering an enterprise-wide application Desired Qualifications: Experience supporting an enterprise-wide student information system Demonstrated experience maintaining application integration and data flow management An understanding of admissions and/or enrollment related business processes (e.g., recruiting, application review, decisions) Ability to manage complex tasks with minimal supervision in team situation and communicate effectively with broad range of individuals Other Qualifications: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States.  Visa sponsorship and relocation allowance are not available for this position. Report to work obligations to support the department and may require work during HPU’s winter break, if necessary. This position may be considered an essential position with report to work obligations depending on the type of emergency, campus closure, or evacuation. Must meet training and background check qualifications and comply with the Protection of Minors policy. Upon hire , must maintain reliable personal transportation to facilitate travel between to all HPU worksites and other locations as required by the position . This includes a valid driver’s license and a personal vehicle that is legally registered and insured. Able to work all shifts and extended hours, as applicable. Ability to work in a fast - paced environment requiring excellent time and stress management skills. Key Responsibilities/Essential Job Functions: 1. Tech Support and Consultation to assigned functional area SIS, FIS or HRIS (45%) Participate and manage software development for systems integration projects, data analytics and extraction, data cleanup, and software solutions related to business process changes. Analyze system, user, and project requirements; design, develop, test, and implement related solutions. Routinely monitor for application issues. Investigate, identify, and implement appropriate solutions. Develop and maintain written documentation for all designated area-related application processes and ensure that information about new software releases is communicated to end users. Create and run queries and audit data in the designated Banner module on a regular basis. Evaluate departmental needs and research solutions Provide daily technical support, user support, and training on designated ERP module and related software; participate in Banner project team(s) or task forces as required; monitor and communicate process or system changes to impacted parties and process owners. Assist the designated department with system revisions and integration; testing designated department systems and processes during upgrades and enhancements. Create and define test plans and validation points. Provide information and training to the designated department staff on system design/utilization/upgrades; assist with general problem solving and inquiries. Manage designated department related tools, including Banner, customer relationship management systems, electronic workflows, operational data stores, report writers, etc.  Such management includes data maintenance, system configuration, data imports and exports, report creation, form creation, workflow development, communications management, user account administration, etc. Communicate regularly with users to identify business requirements; develop and implement ways to use various systems to meet such requirements, performing gap analysis and interfacing with vendors on enhancements to address gaps. Manage the University’s payment system, including upgrade, troubleshooting , integration with third party applications. 2. Software/Data Administration (45%) Understand data access and integration needs of the various enterprise systems such as LMS, CRM, in-house custom apps, etc. used by students, faculty, and staff. Actively participate in application development to provide expertise in building well-designed and implemented processes. Recommend new technologies and strategies that will improve work processes, advance the goals of the University, and convert legacy applications as needed. Be responsible for managing a wide variety of applications and middleware related to designated department functions. Provide trend analysis on the helpdesk systems to identify problem areas and recommend solutions to increase productivity and to improve efficiencies. Provision/de-provision user access to ERP systems, LMS, CRM, CMS, door access control systems, etc. Perform access audit on these systems on a regular basis. Design, implement and support solutions related to critical ad hoc requests. Most of these solutions will need to be production ready in a short time-frame . Manage data flow and data integrity according to HPU standards. Work with other IT teams to ensure compliance with various statutes and rules such as GLBA and FTC Safeguards Rules. Coordinate with external auditors to perform annual audits. Support the IT Cybersecurity team by providing log analysis, critical system patching and information gathering. 3.  Performs other related duties as assigned (10%) Work with other University teams to coordinate projects through project review meetings, status updates, reports on problems and resolutions, and recommendations concerning assigned activities in order to enhance the effectiveness of student intake. Attend technical training courses to enhance knowledge of programming and computer skills and techniques across platforms. Perform miscellaneous administrative duties, including maintaining technical documentation, and providing expertise and assistance to other staff. Actively participates as an effective member of team by completing assigned duties, accepting additional assignments or reassignments. This description is not designed to list all activities, duties or responsibilities which may be required for this job. Other duties, responsibilities and activities may be assigned at any time. Hawaii Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a diverse, equitable environment in which faculty and staff can excel irrespective of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, or any other protected class covered by state and federal law. Hawaii Pacific University encourages applications from veterans and individuals with disabilities. A pre-employment background investigation is performed on candidates selected for employment. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants, including individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), reasonable accommodations are available throughout the application and hiring process. If you require an accommodation, please contact hr@hpu.edu to request assistance. Hawai'i Pacific University is a learning community where staff, faculty, and more than 5,000 students come together from around the world to learn and work in a spirit of caring, honesty, freedom, and 'ohana (family). Cooperation, communication, and collegiality are the foundation of our community. We fulfill the responsibilities of our educational mission through mutual trust and respect, innovation and involvement, expertise, and intellectual fellowship. We offer all members of our community the opportunity to excel, including resources and rewards commensurate with individual contributions and potential. As a team, we are committed to serving our local and global communities and embrace our values of aloha, pono, and kuleana. We seek talented and energetic people who thrive on challenge and innovation in supporting the mission and values of our university. HPU offers competitive compensation and a comprehensive benefits package. For student employment, please visit Career Development Center . Why consider a career with HPU?  Here are some of the benefits of employment . . . Time Off A generous schedule that recognizes 15 holidays annually, plus winter break days off between Christmas and New Year's.  Eligible employees also receive vacation, sick and other types of paid leave. Tuition Waiver Full time employees and spouse/dependent children pursuing a higher education degree at HPU may apply for a tuition waiver. Health and Wellness Comprehensive health insurance, life and disability insurance, employee assistance program and wellness program. Retirement Plan Eligible employees can start saving for the future and enroll in the Hawai'i Pacific University 403(b) retirement plan upon hire. Discounts Discounts for products and services including airlines, rental car, hotels, theme parks, attractions, gift cards, restaurants, and more. 01 Do you have a bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Management Information Systems, Business Administration, or a related field, or at least three (3) years of relevant IT experience in lieu of a degree? Yes No 02 Do you have experience working within fully integrated systems, including applications, databases, and/or application program interfaces (APIs)? Yes No 03 Do you have professional experience administering or supporting an enterprise-wide application used across multiple departments or business functions? Yes No Required Question Employer Hawaii Pacific University Address Waterfront Plaza 500 Ala Moana Blvd Ste 4-545 Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Phone 8085441188 Website http://www.hpu.edu/jobs Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. 